cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "A structured research program on the Riemann hypothesis"
message: "If you use this repository or the papers in it, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tyagi
    given-names: Kunal
    email: hello.jay.tyagi@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/x67ai/riemann-rh-program"
abstract: >-
  The complete record of a structured research program on the Riemann hypothesis: four
  negative results with their proofs, pre-registered decision procedures, adversarial
  reviews, primary-source citation verification, raw data, and a Lean 4 formalization of
  twelve theorems. The mathematics was produced by Claude (Anthropic) working under the
  author's direction; the author set the objectives, adjudicated the decisions, and is
  responsible for the content. Claude is a tool and is not an author.
keywords:
  - Riemann hypothesis
  - analytic number theory
  - pair correlation
  - Lean 4
  - formalized mathematics
  - negative results
  - reproducible research
